    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 lineup today is headlined by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (78.06) and **Gunnar Henderson** (77.04), both of whom offer the highest efficiency floor against favorable matchups. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a distinct platoon edge against Anderson, while **Gunnar Henderson** thrives in a high-park-factor environment against Perkins, whose 3.79 xERA is the most dangerous on today\u2019s slate but mitigated by **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s massive +14% platoon boost. We are also projecting significant upside from **Kyle Tucker** (76.12) and **Jackson Merrill** (69.87), as both players leverage favorable SP skill differentials to anchor our offense. **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Miguel Vargas** (63.69) represent tactical plays; specifically, **Miguel Vargas** earns a nod due to a generous +19% SP skill adjustment and a stolen base opportunity against a pitcher with a notably slow delivery, critical in our effort to maintain dominance in the league's scarcest category.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Wade Meckler**, who fell just shy of the 40-point efficiency floor at 28.48. While his contact profile remains intriguing, a difficult L/L platoon matchup against S\u00e1nchez, C and an unfavorable #9 batting order slot relegated him to the bench to preserve our game caps. Meanwhile, **Luis Robert Jr.** remains inactive and off the board, and we continue to monitor the long-term statuses of **Andy Pages** and **Jacob Wilson** on the IL. We are rolling with **Drake Baldwin** at catcher today\u2014his 67.93 score is heavily bolstered by his leadoff position and a favorable matchup against Agnos. No immediate weather alerts are flagged for the current slate, though we advise monitoring the lineups for **Dominic Smith** and **Nasim Nunez** to ensure no late-scratch defensive substitutions impact their expected volume.",
